{
  "id": 204613826,
  "iid": 9764,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Sharkd: Add Zero padding to RGB colors displayed in frames",
  "description": "The `color_t_to_rgb` method returns an unsigned int, taking a 32-bit\ncolor code and reducing it to an integer. Sharkd displays these as hex\ncolors compatible with CSS rules.\n\nHowever, if this color is missing a Red or Green component, the hex\noutput is missing the zero-padding for those parts of the color,\nresulting in the wrong or invalid hex code when interpreted as-is.\n\nThis MR pads the color output with zeros.\n\n### Sharkd Example\n\n(Assumes a color rule with a full-blue background color ie. `@TCP RST@tcp.flags.reset eq 1@[0,0,65535][65535,64764,40092]`)\n\n```json\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"frames\",\"params\":{\"skip\":62, \"limit\":1}}\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"result\":[{\"c\":[\"63\",\"42.541697\",\"10.20.30.1\",\"10.20.30.42\",\"TCP\",\"60\",\"88 → 49671 [RST, ACK] Seq=222 Ack=243 Win=0 Len=0\"],\"num\":63,\"bg\":\"0000ff\",\"fg\":\"fffc9c\"}]}\n```",
  "state": "merged",
